<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jang Mun-hyu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jang Mun-hyu was a general of Balhae who in 732, on the orders of King Mu, led a fleet across the Bohai Sea and attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dengzhou">Dengzhou</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> peninsula, killing its Tang prefect. The raid, part of a conflict caused by Balhae's war on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heishui-mohe">Heishui Mohe</a> and the flight of Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-munye">Dae Munye</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, was a rare seaborne attack on Tang territory.</p></div>
